<nav class="container breadcrumbs" aria-label="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a><span>›</span> Sustainability</nav>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container reveal">
    <h2>Conservation & environmental awareness</h2>
    <p>The tour is also an educational experience: you'll learn about the ecology of guano birds, Humboldt penguins and the sea-lion colony, observing wildlife <strong>without interfering with their habitat</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--warm">
  <div class="container reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our practices</p>
    <h2>Our environmental commitments</h2>
    <p class="lead">We operate with a low-impact, sustainability-first approach, backed by concrete practices aboard our vessels.</p>
    <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:var(--space-6)">
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>No single-use plastic</h3><p>We have progressively eliminated single-use plastic: drinks are served in <strong>reusable ceramic mugs</strong> and, when needed, in biodegradable paper cups.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Zero waste into the sea</h3><p>Throwing <strong>any waste into the sea is strictly forbidden</strong>. All waste generated on board is taken back to shore for proper disposal, with separated bins used throughout the voyage.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Efficient water use</h3><p>We control the use of drinking water during service and cleaning, and we promote responsible water use among passengers and crew.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Responsible drink service</h3><p>Hot and cold drinks are prepared only on request and according to the actual number of passengers, avoiding waste of supplies and food.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top-gold"><div class="card__body"><h3>SERNANP fee</h3><p>An official contribution to conserving the National Reserve.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Environmental awareness</h3><p>We inform passengers about good practices on board and regularly train our crew in sustainability and waste management.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--sky">
  <div class="container reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Waste management</p>
    <h2>Learn to separate your waste</h2>
    <p class="lead">Separating waste correctly makes reuse and recycling easier and reduces the extraction of natural resources from the ecosystem. On board you'll find separated bins:</p>
    <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:var(--space-6)">
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Recyclable waste</h3><p>Plastic, glass, cardboard and metals. Remember to rinse them before discarding.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Organic waste</h3><p>Food scraps.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Non-recoverable waste</h3><p>Used tissues, face masks, and paper or cardboard soiled with food.</p></div></div>
      <div class="card card--top"><div class="card__body"><h3>Paper waste</h3><p>Exclusively for clean paper waste.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:var(--space-6);font-weight:600">Let's take care of the sea together: drop your waste in the bins and help protect marine life.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container reveal">
    <h2>Within a National Reserve</h2>
    <p>We operate in the National Reserve System of Islands, Islets and Guano Capes, under the SERNANP framework. Our food-waste prevention and waste-management practices are aligned with the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>
